<title>HONG KONG: Tysan year net profit rises 21 percent.</title>
<headline>Tysan year net profit rises 21 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   20.9   vs 17.5</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    5.0    vs 2.4</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs 29.28 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    85.00  vs 70.09</p>
<p>    Turnover		     880.70 vs 405.11</p>
<p>    Company name		 Tysan Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 19-26</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 18</p>
<p>NOTE - Tysan is engaged in the foundation piling business, property development and machinery hiring.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one-for-10 shares and one 1998 warrant for every 10 shares held.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is seven cents (including interim dividend of two cents) vs 3.6 cents.</p>
<p>-- HK Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
